{
  "body_human_readable": "**\"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" (2005): A Look at Its Financial Journey**\n\nThe 2005 film adaptation of Douglas Adams' beloved science fiction series, \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,\" was produced with a budget estimated to be between $45 and $50 million. The movie went on to achieve a worldwide box office gross of approximately $104.5 million.\n\nThe film, which was released in the United Kingdom on April 28, 2005, and a day later in North America, opened in the top spot at the North American box office with an opening weekend gross of about $21.1 million. In the United States, it remained in the top ten for its first four weeks of release. The total worldwide earnings were composed of $51,085,416 from the domestic market and $53,393,000 from international markets.",
